      "title": "Self-inflicted injury and war",
      "narration": "Policies exclude intentionally self-inflicted injuries, including injuries from a suicide attempt, because insurance covers accidental and unexpected loss. Mental health treatment for the underlying condition is a separate, covered matter under parity rules. Policies also exclude losses caused by war or an act of war, declared or undeclared, and often losses while serving in the armed forces, for which military coverage exists. If Rosa deliberately injures herself, her disability policy does not pay; if she is injured in a terrorist attack at home, most policies pay because that is not war between nations.",
