      "title": "Cosmetic versus reconstructive",
      "narration": "Elective cosmetic surgery, chosen to change appearance without a medical need, is excluded. Reconstructive surgery is different. Repairing a face after an accident, correcting a congenital defect in a child, or rebuilding a breast after a mastectomy restores function or appearance lost to injury or disease, and these are covered. Maryland specifically requires coverage of reconstructive breast surgery after a mastectomy, including surgery on the other breast for symmetry. The question to ask is why the procedure is being done. A medical cause moves the claim out of the exclusion.",
