      "narration": "Injuries sustained while committing or attempting a felony, or while engaged in an illegal occupation, are excluded. The uniform optional provision on illegal occupation, which Lesson 17 covers, lets the insurer deny a loss arising from such activity. A person injured while burglarizing a warehouse cannot collect medical or disability benefits for those injuries. The exclusion requires participation in the crime; a bystander or victim injured during someone else’s felony is covered. Some policies similarly exclude losses while intoxicated or under the influence of unprescribed narcotics, again through an optional provision.",
